/*
 * DankMango GTK3 live-theme shadow  --  GENERATED, do not edit by hand.
 *
 * Installed to: ~/.local/share/themes/@THEME@/gtk-3.0/@LEAF@
 * Regenerate with: install.sh (stage 9)
 *
 * WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
 * --------------------
 * Changing the wallpaper used to require restarting Nemo (and every other GTK3
 * app) before the new matugen colours showed up. This file is what removes that
 * restart. It is not a cosmetic layer -- it is the whole mechanism.
 *
 * GTK3 has two separate CSS load paths and they behave completely differently:
 *
 *   1. The USER stylesheet, ~/.config/gtk-3.0/gtk.css, is read ONCE when the
 *      process starts and is never re-read. Nothing -- no gsettings key, no
 *      xdg-desktop-portal signal, no file-monitor inside GTK -- makes a running
 *      app pick up an edit to it. (Verified on GTK 3.24 and 4.22.)
 *
 *   2. A NAMED THEME (this file) is re-loaded from disk every time the
 *      org.gnome.desktop.interface gtk-theme key changes -- and the reload
 *      follows @import, so an imported file that changed on disk comes back
 *      fresh too.
 *
 * DMS already flips gtk-theme to "" and back on every wallpaper change (its
 * refreshGTK() in core/internal/matugen/matugen.go). Historically that flip did
 * nothing useful, because the colours lived in the user stylesheet at path 1.
 * Moving the matugen palette down into path 2 turns that existing flip into a
 * genuine live reload: no restart, no new daemon, no file watcher.
 *
 * The two imports below are ordered deliberately:
 *   - the packaged adw-gtk3 theme first, for all the widget rules and its
 *     relative assets .svg|png references (checkmarks, radio bullets, slider
 *     handles -- they resolve against /usr/share/themes/..., where they live);
 *   - dank-colors.css second, so its @define-color values win and recolour
 *     everything the theme just defined.
 *
 * The counterpart to this file is ~/.config/gtk-3.0/gtk.css, which must NOT
 * import dank-colors.css. The user stylesheet outranks the theme, so a stale
 * copy of the palette at that level shadows the fresh values here and silently
 * defeats the whole thing.
 *
 * NOT APPLICABLE TO GTK4: GTK4 ignores custom named themes at runtime entirely,
 * so GTK4 apps (Celluloid, Loupe) still need a restart. See docs/GUIDE.md.
 */
@import url("file:///usr/share/themes/@THEME@/gtk-3.0/@LEAF@");
@import url("file://@COLORS@");
